--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6BitNBPiv`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Bit.NB.edge_of_pivs (hm : 1 < m) (q : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin m) ℚ) (hq : q * q = q)
--       (rs : List (ℕ × ℕ × ℕ)) (hok : ∀ ρ ∈ rs, RunOK m ρ) (hnd : (runPairs rs).Nodup)
--       (hp : ∀ x ∈ runPairs rs, IsPiv q x.1 x.2) :
--       ∃ e : Edge m, (∃ rs', e.runs = rs ++ rs' ∧ (∀ ρ ∈ rs', ρ.2.2 = 1) ∧
--           (runPairs rs).length + rs'.length = q.rank) ∧
--         (∀ ρ ∈ e.runs, RunOK m ρ) ∧
--         (∀ i j, i < j → e.E₁ i j = 0) ∧ (∀ i, e.E₁ i i ≠ 0) ∧
--         (∀ i j, i < j → e.E₂ i j = 0) ∧ (∀ i, e.E₂ i i ≠ 0) ∧
--         e.E₁ * ((e.runs.flatMap (runPiv m)).map fun p => Equiv.swap p.1 p.2).prod.permMatrix ℚ *
--           e.E₂ = pswQ q
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, bit network: pivots from ranks, and edges from pivots
--
--   * `rk q X Y`: rank of the rows `< X`, columns `≥ Y` of `q`; `IsPiv q i j`: the
--     inclusion–exclusion of `rk` at `(i, j)` is one.
--   * `isPiv_iff`: for a Bruhat factorization `E₁ P E₂`, `IsPiv` is exactly `P i j = 1`.
--   * `edge_of_pivs`: for an idempotent `q` over `ℚ` and runs whose positions are pivots of `q`, there
--     is an edge (lower triangular `E₁, E₂`, nonzero diagonals) with runs `rs ++ rs'`, `rs'` singletons,
--     `|rs| + |rs'| = rank q`, and frame `E₁ σ E₂ = pswQ q` (the partial swap of `q`).
